        "kind": "example",
        "title": "For any field $F$, $(F, +)$ and $(F \\setminus \\{0\\}, \\cdot)$ are abelian groups; in particular $(\\mathbb{Q}, +)$, $(\\mathbb{Q} \\setminus \\{0\\}, \\cdot)$, $(\\mathbb{R}, +)$ and $(\\mathbb{R} \\setminus \\{0\\}, \\cdot)$",
