      {
        "id": "ex-integers-mod-n-additive-group",
        "kind": "example",
        "title": "For $n \\ge 1$ the congruence classes modulo $n$ form an abelian group $(\\mathbb{Z}/n, +)$ of order $n$, generated by the class of $1$",
        "strategy": "direct",
        "deps": [
